  "reviewScope": "Root read all twelve final-local contract narratives, eighteen parser specializations, nine lead corrections, cross-owner dispositions and original assertion associations. Completeness verification and eight-file independent sampling do not claim root reread every native/source line.",
  "qualifications": [
    {
      "id": "PF-ROOT-CACHE-REMOVE",
      "detail": "Identity guard applies to prune eviction, not every removal. TypeScript forgetWindowTarget directly deletes computed aliases; preserve a separate test for stale invalidation versus a newer alias. Explicit-namespace writes add global canonical keys in TypeScript but not Swift; explicit lookups still avoid global fallback. Do not generalize this into proven cross-session exploitation."
    },
    {
      "id": "PF-ROOT-CACHE-PERSIST",
      "detail": "Schema2 shallow session object admission allows arrays; appVersion merely string. mkdir/write modes are creation arguments, not hardening existing directories/files or Windows ACL proof. Startup temp sweeping can remove another instance's pending save. Source control flow, not permission or durability execution."
    },
    {
      "id": "PF-ROOT-GESTURE",
      "detail": "After final point index reaches length, close clears timer but neither resolves nor rejects; both before next 16ms callback and during final 50ms grace can remain pending. Original single happy-path socket test was read, not executed, and does not cover close races. A completed send is not device effect acknowledgment."
    },
    {
      "id": "PF-ROOT-SIMBOOT",
      "detail": "ensureSimulatorBooted falls through successfully after 22s polling deadline without a Booted observation. Boot attempt errors are swallowed before polling. No actual simulator launch ran; characterize historical behavior separately from intended timeout rejection."
    },
    {
      "id": "PF-ROOT-NATIVE-TEXT",
      "detail": "Swift AX replacement can succeed and then return nil on unmatched readback, activating synthetic typing/paste fallback after an effect. Native setValue can return verified readback. AX scroll ignores per-action false. These source observations do not establish live OS reproduction or authorize duplicate effects."
    }
  ],
